- `action(n7, "end process after organizing team")`, `action(n8, "end process after contacting customer")`: Hallucinated steps; the description states the process simply "will come to an end" immediately after "organize a suitable team" or "contact the customer directly", without intermediate termination actions.
- `branch(b1)` / missing `guard` statements: Omitted decision conditions; the model declares an XOR split but fails to provide `guard(...)` statements to associate the outgoing edges with the source conditions "contract is deemed okay" and "missing details".
- `defines(v1, "is contract okay", {})`: Unfaithful variable definition; the value range is an empty set `{}` rather than capturing the mutually exclusive decision states implied by the branching logic.
- `action(n4, "is contract okay")`: Misrepresented node semantics; evaluating the contract is a control-flow condition, not an executable process step, and should be integrated into the branch/guard logic instead of modeled as a standalone action preceding `branch(b1)`.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S2] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n5` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.